# Gitignored local files that worktree-creating tools copy into a new worktree.
# Patterns use .gitignore syntax; tracked files are never duplicated.
#
# Claude Code honours this convention. GitHub Copilot CLI does not, so a
# Copilot-created worktree still starts without these files — see
# docs/development/local-setup.md § Git worktrees and `.env`.
#
# Deliberately minimal: developer credentials only. Never add dependencies,
# build output, or branch state — copying those defeats the point of a clean
# worktree.
.env
